to restore a game
  NETHACK -U charactername -R
 not obvious, I know...  I had to ask nethack to tell me (NETHACK -?)

when you read a scroll, it sometimes gives a description of what it does,
aloowing you to give it a name so that you'll know what it does next time
you find the same type of scroll..  same thing goes for potions...
e.g. if you read a scroll, and the description says "you hear maniacal
laughter", you can name the scroll "laughter" (this is a 'scare monster'
scroll, if I remember right)... or if you quaff a blue potion and it
says "This is GOOD stuff *hick*" you can bet it's alcoholic and name
the potion appropriately...  if you don't name the items, the next time
you'll still get just a blue potion or a scroll of FOOBIE BLECH, and you
may not remember what it does...

